// Both the callee and the argument are wrong. Each side knows both facts, so what
// is pinned here is the ORDER: the reference elaborates a call's arguments before
// resolving its callee, and reports the argument.
//
// The two controls live in the corpus already as separate fixtures - a known
// callee with a bad argument, and an unknown callee with a good one - and both
// agreed all along. Only the crossing diverged, which is what makes this an order
// question rather than a wording one.
fn main() { println(nope_f(nope_a)); }
